'''Sāmbār''', or '''sambhar''', is a [[lentil]]-based vegetable spiced [[curry]] or [[stew]], cooked with [[pigeon pea]]s and [[tamarind]] [[broth]]. It originates in [[South Indian cuisine]] and is also eaten in other parts of India.
